Relevant columns, their potential usage and typical conditions
--------------------------------------------------------------
• event_name: filter to the commerce event that represents a completed order.  
  Condition → WHERE event_name = 'purchase'

• event_date: lets us translate every row into calendar months.  
  Condition → WHERE event_date BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20210131'

• user_pseudo_id: pseudonymous customer identifier that ties all events of the same user together.  
  Usage → GROUP BY / IN (…) to find everything a customer bought after we know she bought the tee.

• items (REPEATED RECORD)
  – items.item_name   : the product’s name (e.g. “Google Red Speckled Tee”).  
  – items.quantity    : number of units purchased.  
  Condition → UNNEST(items) AS i … WHERE LOWER(i.item_name) = 'google red speckled tee'

