Relevant columns, their potential usage and typical conditions
--------------------------------------------------------------
• event_name: filter to the commerce event that represents a completed order.  
  Condition → WHERE event_name = 'purchase'

• event_date: lets us translate every row into calendar months.  
  Condition → WHERE event_date BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20210131'

• user_pseudo_id: pseudonymous customer identifier that ties all events of the same user together.  
  Usage → GROUP BY / IN (…) to find everything a customer bought after we know she bought the tee.

• items (REPEATED RECORD)
  – items.item_name   : the product’s name (e.g. “Google Red Speckled Tee”).  
  – items.quantity    : number of units purchased.  
  Condition → UNNEST(items) AS i … WHERE LOWER(i.item_name) = 'google red speckled tee'

10 progressively richer exploratory queries
-------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Quick look at which event types exist on one day
SELECT DISTINCT event_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201109`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect a handful of purchase rows to discover product field names
SELECT event_date,
       user_pseudo_id,
       items
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201109`
WHERE event_name = 'purchase'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. All distinct product names that contain "tee" (case‑insensitive) on 9‑Nov‑2020
SELECT DISTINCT i.item_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201109`,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE LOWER(i.item_name) LIKE '%tee%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Find users who bought the Google Red Speckled Tee on 9‑Nov‑2020
SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201109`,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE event_name = 'purchase'
  AND LOWER(i.item_name) = 'google red speckled tee'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Inspect the other products those same customers bought on that day
SELECT u.user_pseudo_id,
       other.item_name,
       other.quantity
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201109` AS u
JOIN UNNEST(u.items) AS tee
     ON LOWER(tee.item_name) = 'google red speckled tee'
JOIN UNNEST(u.items) AS other
     ON TRUE
WHERE u.event_name = 'purchase'
  AND LOWER(other.item_name) <> 'google red speckled tee'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Users who bought the tee anywhere in November‑2020
SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20201130'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND LOWER(i.item_name) = 'google red speckled tee'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Quantity of *other* products these users bought during November‑2020
SELECT other.item_name,
       SUM(other.quantity) AS qty
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
     UNNEST(items) AS other
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20201130'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND user_pseudo_id IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
             UNNEST(items) AS i
        WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20201130'
          AND event_name = 'purchase'
          AND LOWER(i.item_name) = 'google red speckled tee'
      )
  AND LOWER(other.item_name) <> 'google red speckled tee'
GROUP BY other.item_name
ORDER BY qty DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same aggregation for December‑2020
SELECT other.item_name,
       SUM(other.quantity) AS qty
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
     UNNEST(items) AS other
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND user_pseudo_id IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
             UNNEST(items) AS i
        WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201201' AND '20201231'
          AND event_name = 'purchase'
          AND LOWER(i.item_name) = 'google red speckled tee'
      )
  AND LOWER(other.item_name) <> 'google red speckled tee'
GROUP BY other.item_name
ORDER BY qty DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Check how many tee‑buyers we have in each month (Nov‑20, Dec‑20, Jan‑21)
SELECT FORMAT_DATE('%Y‑%m', PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d', event_date)) AS month,
       COUNT(DISTINCT user_pseudo_id) AS tee_buyers
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
     UNNEST(items) AS i
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20210131'
  AND event_name = 'purchase'
  AND LOWER(i.item_name) = 'google red speckled tee'
GROUP BY month
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER – Most purchased *other* product (and its total quantity)
--     by customers who bought the Google Red Speckled Tee
--     for November‑2020, December‑2020, January‑2021
SELECT month,
       item_name,
       total_qty
FROM (
  SELECT
    FORMAT_DATE('%Y‑%m', PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d', event_date)) AS month,
    other.item_name,
    SUM(other.quantity) AS total_qty,
    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY FORMAT_DATE('%Y‑%m', PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d', event_date))
                       ORDER BY SUM(other.quantity) DESC) AS rk
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
       UNNEST(items) AS other
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20210131'
    AND event_name = 'purchase'
    AND user_pseudo_id IN (
          SELECT DISTINCT user_pseudo_id
          FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_*`,
               UNNEST(items) AS i
          WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20201101' AND '20210131'
            AND event_name = 'purchase'
            AND LOWER(i.item_name) = 'google red speckled tee'
        )
    AND LOWER(other.item_name) <> 'google red speckled tee'
  GROUP BY month, other.item_name
)
WHERE rk = 1
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

The last query returns, for each of the three months (2020‑11, 2020‑12, 2021‑01), the single “most purchased other product” together with the total quantity bought by all customers who purchased the Google Red Speckled Tee during the same month.
